<title>USA: Reno Air May load factor 66.9 vs 65.</title>
<headline>Reno Air May load factor 66.9 vs 65.</headline>
<dateline>RENO, Nev. 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reno Air Inc. Monday reported a 66.9 percent load factor for May, which is an increase of 1.9 load factor points over May, 1996.</p>
<p>The low fare, full service airline carried 457,707 passengers, an increase of 5.3 percent over the same period last year, and flew 257,386,631 revenue passenger miles (RPMs) with a capacity of 384,757,726 available seat miles (ASMs).</p>
<p>				 RENO AIR TRAFFIC STATISTICS</p>
<p>					  MAY 1997	  MAY 1996  PERCENT CHANGE</p>
<p>    RPMs (000)			 257,387	   256,220	.5%</p>
<p>    ASMs (000)			 384,758	   394,450    (2.5)%</p>
<p>    Load Factor (%)		     66.9		65.0     1.9 points</p>
<p>    Passengers			 457,707	   434,622     5.3%</p>
<p>					   YEAR-TO-DATE</p>
<p>				     PERIOD ENDED MAY 31</p>
<p>				     MAY 31, 1997     MAY 31, 1996  PERCENT CHANGE</p>
<p>    RPMs (000)		     1,232,046	  1,145,682	7.5%</p>
<p>    ASMs (000)		     1,878,118	  1,720,413	9.2%</p>
<p>    Load Factor (%)		     65.6		 66.6     (1.0) points</p>
<p>    Passengers		     2,172,771	  1,956,393     11.1%</p>
</text>
